From aea0583ffa59b5caa66e6c9f4423745c15e1f47e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 20:10:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] build/webui: remove AiProtection/bwdpi TrendMicro DPI
 (feature-removal Phase 1.2)

Drop BWDPI=y from the RT-BE96U profile in target.mak. All hooks are
RTCONFIG_BWDPI-guarded and compile out; the ~7-8MB TrendMicro vendor
blobs (libbwdpi*, libshn*, dcd, wred, shn_ctrl, tcd, tdts_rule_agent,
tdts*.ko, rule.trf, signatures) no longer stage. Pre-verified safe:
- RTCONFIG_NOTIFICATION_CENTER stays =y via the AMAS profile block.
- Kernel NET_SCH_HTB/SFQ/CAKE/CLS_U32 are native =y in config_base.6a.6813
  (the BWDPI macro only re-appended them) - traditional/limiter/CAKE QoS keep
  their schedulers.
- Blob deps: amas_lib.o + nt_mail.o need check_bwdpi_nvram_setting /
  check_tdts_module_exist / check_wrs_switch = shared/bwdpi_utils.c,
  compiled UNCONDITIONALLY; priv_webapi.o needs dump_dpi_support =
  ASUS's own #ifndef RTCONFIG_BWDPI stub in libwebapi/webapi.c. No
  un-gating needed this time.
- GUI: menuTree auto-hides AiProtection/AdaptiveQoS/TrafficAnalyzer and
  falls back to the traditional QoS menu. AiProtection pages stay staged
  (DNSQUERY_INTERCEPT=y skips the www rm block) but are menu-hidden.
Loses (accepted): Adaptive QoS, AiProtection IPS/malware blocking, App
Patrol, Web History, Traffic Analyzer stats. Keeps: HW QoS 10/11,
Traditional/Bandwidth-Limiter/CAKE, Traffic Monitor (rstats), time-based
Parental Controls (pc.c), dns_dpi (DNSQUERY_INTERCEPT).

Reaper dashboard rail updated: AiProtection link removed; Parental
Controls -> ParentalControl.asp; Adaptive QoS -> QoS_EZQoS.asp ('QoS');
Traffic Analyzer -> Main_TrafficMonitor_realtime.asp ('Traffic Monitor');
also removed the stale Amazon Alexa link missed in Phase 1.1 (page was
deleted in 492b2efd25).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
